.TH SDL_MAIN_HANDLED 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_MAIN_HANDLED \- Inform SDL that the app is providing an entry point instead of SDL.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_main.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_MAIN_HANDLED 1
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
SDL does not define this macro, but will check if it is defined when including
.BR SDL_main\[char46]h \[char46]
If defined, SDL will expect the app to provide the proper entry point for the platform, and all the other magic details needed, like manually calling
.BR SDL_SetMainReady \[char46]
.PP
Please see [README-main-functions](README-main-functions), (or docs/README-main-functions\[char46]md in the source tree) for a more detailed explanation\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is used by the headers since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

